            0.138,
            0.11,
            0.881,
            0.15
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. The height of a cone is 16 cm, and its base radius is 12 cm. Find the curved surface area and the total surface area of the cone."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.138,
            0.154,
            0.881,
            0.192
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. A cone has a height of 15 cm. If its volume is 1570 cm"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3",
              "styles": [
                "superscript"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ", find the radius of the base."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.138,
            0.198,
            0.882,
            0.256
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. The curved surface area of a cone is 308 cm"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2",
              "styles": [
                "superscript"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and its slant height is 14 cm. Find (i) the radius of the base, (ii) the total surface area of the cone."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.138,
            0.261,
            0.881,
            0.32
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "6. A joker’s cap is in the form of a right circular cone of base radius 7 cm and height 24 cm. Find the area of the sheet required to make 10 such caps."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.129,
            0.324,
            0.882,
            0.403
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "*7. What length of tarpaulin 3 m wide is required to make a conical tent of height 8 m and base radius 6 m? Assume that the extra length of material that is required for stitching margins and wastage in cutting is 20 cm."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.14,
            0.407,
            0.881,
            0.464
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "8. A right triangle with sides 6 cm, 8 cm and 10 cm is rotated through 360° about the side of 8 cm. Find the volume and the curved surface area of the solid so formed."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.469,
            0.652,
            0.569
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "*9. Suppose you have a cup in the shape of a right circular cone. Fill it with water to half the depth of the cone. What fraction of the volume of the cup is occupied by the water?"
            }
          ]
        },
